# SABOTAGE: the SILENT-EMPTY-FUNNEL verifier's mount MATCHER
# (`Mix.Tasks.Samen.Verify.AnalyticsProducer.reader_call?/1`, ADR-021 / mount-ledger
# Amendment 3). Neutering BOTH clauses to `false` models the exact vacuous-gate regression this
# class of verifier is prone to: the AST scan stops recognising a real
# `samen_tenant_analytics_routes/2` CALL, so `reader_mount` is `[]` for every app, the
# reader=>producer obligation is never ENGAGED, and the verifier prints "OK — no violations"
# over a host that mounts the analytics reader with no product-event producer (the samenerp
# defect, now invisible). The GREEN non-vacuity assertion and the RED emitter assertion both
# flip, which is what the MUST_FAIL below detects: a matcher that silently matches nothing
# must never read as "no violation".
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/analytics_producer_verifier_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED (emitter): reader mounted, no product_event_resource is one violation
--- a/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.analytics_producer.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.analytics_producer.ex
@@ -363,8 +363,8 @@
   # {:\\, _, [{:opts, _, nil}, []]}]}` — a FIRST argument variable and a SECOND argument
   # that is a `:\\` node, never a keyword list — so requiring a keyword-list second
   # argument (or the one-arg form) excludes the definition while matching every real mount.
-  defp reader_call?({@reader_macro, _meta, [_namespace]}), do: true
-  defp reader_call?({@reader_macro, _meta, [_namespace, opts]}), do: is_list(opts)
+  defp reader_call?({@reader_macro, _meta, [_namespace]}), do: false
+  defp reader_call?({@reader_macro, _meta, [_namespace, _opts]}), do: false
   defp reader_call?(_), do: false
 
